<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Li Jishen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1885">1885</a>–<a href="/years/1959">1959</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Li Jishen was a Chinese general and politician of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomintang">Kuomintang</a> who repeatedly broke with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chiang-kai-shek">Chiang Kai-shek</a>. In 1933 he joined the leaders of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/19th-route-army">19th Route Army</a> in proclaiming the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fujian">Fujian</a> People's Government, which was quickly crushed. He later founded the Revolutionary Committee of the Kuomintang and became a vice-chairman of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-republic-of-china">People's Republic of China</a>'s government after 1949.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/li-jishen.jpg" alt="Li Jishen" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%9D%8E%E6%B5%8E%E6%B7%B1%E5%B0%86%E5%86%9B.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
